  "title": "Ricotta Gnudi with Fermented Black Garlic",
  "image": "generated://dishcovery/9000019.jpg",
  "readyInMinutes": 50,
  "servings": 4,
  "summary": "Elevate your pasta night with these pillowy Italian gnudi dumplings that highlight <b>a savory fermented black garlic compound</b>. Soft ricotta cheese is whipped with aged parmesan, egg yolks, and fine semolina flour before being gently folded around sweet, earthy paste made from long-fermented garlic cloves. Poached delicate dough balls float effortlessly to the surface of simmering water, yielding an remarkably light bite that bursts with rich umami depth. A minimal emulsion of sage-infused brown butter complements the fermented garlic without overpowering its subtle caramel undertones. This sophisticated dish bridges traditional Tuscan dumpling craft with contemporary flavor complexity, making it an extraordinary choice for dinner parties. Resting the uncooked dumplings overnight in semolina allows a delicate skin to form, ensuring they hold their round structure flawlessly when submerged in the hot poaching bath.",
